@echo off
echo [*] Zurvan Installation Script for Windows
echo.
echo Note: Zurvan is primarily designed for Linux environments due to its heavy reliance on network tools like Scapy, Aircrack-ng, and iptables/tun interfaces.
echo For the best experience on Windows, we strongly recommend using WSL2 (Windows Subsystem for Linux) with Kali Linux or Ubuntu.
echo.
echo If you wish to proceed on Windows natively:
echo 1. Install Python 3.10+ from python.org.
echo 2. Install Npcap (ensure 'Install Npcap in WinPcap API-compatible Mode' is checked).
echo 3. Install Visual C++ Build Tools.
echo 4. Run: pip install -r requirements.txt
echo.
echo Many features (WiFi attacks, detailed packet crafting, specific OSINT tools) may NOT work natively on Windows.
echo.
pause
